    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"food_web - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/food_web.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [food_web()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: \"A woodland food web: who eats whom.\"\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [food_web()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: \"A woodland food web: who eats whom.\"\ntitle: >-\n  [food_web()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: \"A woodland food web: who eats whom.\"\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nA woodland food web: who eats whom.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L2360-L2431){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nfood_web()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nSixteen species of a made-up woodland, with an edge from each food to each species that\neats it, so energy flows along the edges from the plants at the bottom to the predators at\nthe top. It's the example for the ecology of networks: trophic levels and how coherent they\nare, the species that reach the most of the web, and what a web loses when one species goes.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 16 nodes (species, labeled by name)\n- 21 edges (from a food to the species that eats it)\n- Directed, acyclic, unweighted\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `kind`: `\"plant\"`, `\"herbivore\"`, `\"omnivore\"` (the jay, which eats acorns and\n  caterpillars) or `\"predator\"`\n- `pos`: an `(x, y)` position for drawing the web, with the plants at the bottom and each\n  animal at a height set by its trophic level\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **Fractional trophic levels.** The plants are at level 1 and the herbivores at level 2.\n  Each other species sits one level above the average of what it eats, so the Jay, eating\n  acorns and caterpillars, is at 2.5, and the Fox, eating frogs, shrews and rabbits, is at\n  3.67, above the Hawk at 3.5.\n- **Top predators.** Nothing eats the Fox, the Hawk or the Marten, so each is an attracting\n  component of its own: once energy reaches one, it goes no further.\n- **A keystone plant.** The Caterpillar and the Squirrel eat nothing but the Oak, the\n  Marten nothing but squirrels, and the Jay only acorns and caterpillars, so losing the Oak\n  starves four more species. Every animal that eats one of the other plants has something\n  else to eat.\n- **Plants that feed the most.** The Grass and the Oak each feed 7 of the other 15\n  species, directly or through what eats them, so their local reaching centrality is\n  `0.467`, the highest in the web.\n- **A tidy hierarchy.** Most feeding links climb one level, but some climb more (the Fox\n  eats rabbits, 1.67 levels down), and the trophic incoherence is `0.28`; a web where every\n  link climbs exactly one level scores `0`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The food web.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the web from the plants up, colored by kind:\n\n::: {#0423cb94 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nweb = ec.food_web()\n\nweb.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"kind\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"14.0 -26.6 802.6 573.3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFo